-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt browser studio
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason’s [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) path tracer, compiled from C++ to WebAssembly with Emscripten. The renderer runs entirely in a module Web Worker; progressive RGBA frames are drawn to a canvas. The home page is prerendered to `dist/client/index.html` by Astro.
 
+- `pnpm install`
+- `pnpm build` — build the application (includes checked-in WebAssembly assets)
+- `pnpm build:wasm` — rebuild the Wasm module with Emscripten (`emcc` required)
 
-```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
-```
+`native/smallpt-original.cpp` retains the upstream source; `native/smallpt.cpp` adds progressive rendering and color exports, preserving the diffuse, mirror, and glass light transport. See `native/LICENSE.txt` for Kevin Beason’s MIT license. Compiled files are in `public/wasm/`. If native source changes, also copy it to `public/native/smallpt.cpp` for the source link.
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+The Randomize colors button tints the walls and both foreground spheres. Quality selection restarts rendering at 16, 64, or 256 samples per pixel; reset restores original materials and colors; Save image downloads the current canvas as PNG. A preview generated with the same C++ implementation appears while the Wasm module loads. No rendering server or cross-origin isolation is required.
 
-## Tech Stack
-
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+To regenerate the initial preview, compile `native/smallpt.cpp` with `g++ -O3 -DSMALLPT_PREVIEW -o /tmp/smallpt-preview`, run that binary, then run `node scripts/build-preview.mjs`.
