+<!doctype html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
+  <meta name="description" content="A tiny path tracer. An entire world of light. Explore Kevin Beason's smallpt running right in your browser with WebAssembly." />
+  <title>smallpt — A little light experiment</title>
+  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
+  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
+  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
+  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;450;500;550;600;650;700&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/studio.css" />
+</head>
+<body>
+<svg class="icon-library" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><symbol id="arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M7 17 17 7M7 7h10v10"/></symbol><symbol id="shuffle" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 6h3c5 0 7 12 12 12h3m-4-4 4 4-4 4M3 18h3c2 0 4-3 6-6s4-6 6-6h3m-4-4 4 4-4 4"/></symbol><symbol id="download" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5M4 15v5h16v-5"/></symbol><symbol id="reset" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 10a8 8 0 1 1 1 7M4 4v6h6"/></symbol><symbol id="code" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m8 7-5 5 5 5m8-10 5 5-5 5m-3-14-2 18"/></symbol><symbol id="cube" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m12 2 9 5v10l-9 5-9-5V7l9-5Zm-9 5 9 5 9-5m-9 5v10M7 4.8l10 5.4"/></symbol></svg>
+<header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="smallpt home"><span class="brand-mark">s<span>p</span></span>smallpt<span class="brand-dot">.</span></a><nav><a href="https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">The original project <svg><use href="#arrow"/></svg></a><a class="source-link" href="/native/smallpt.cpp" target="_blank"><svg><use href="#code"/></svg> View source</a></nav></header>
+<main>
+<section class="intro"><div><div class="eyebrow"><span></span> A LITTLE LIGHT EXPERIMENT</div><h1>Small code.<br/>Infinite <span>possibilities.</span></h1><p>A tiny C++ path tracer, brought to your browser.<br class="desktop-br"/> Play with color. Watch light find its way.</p></div><div class="intro-note"><span class="orbit">✳</span><p>99 lines of C++.<br/>A whole world of light.</p><span class="hand-arrow">↙</span></div></section>
+<section class="studio" aria-label="Path tracing studio">
+<div class="viewport-panel"><div class="viewport-toolbar"><div class="scene-title"><svg><use href="#cube"/></svg> Cornell box <span class="slash">/</span><span>Scene 01</span></div><span class="live-badge"><i></i> LIVE RENDER</span></div>
+<div class="render-area"><img src="/render-preview.png" alt="Path-traced Cornell box with a mirror sphere, a glass sphere, and colored walls" class="preview" /><canvas id="render" width="640" height="480" aria-label="Live smallpt path tracing output"></canvas><span class="canvas-label">PERSPECTIVE CAMERA</span><span class="canvas-corner">640 × 480</span></div>
+<div class="render-footer"><div class="render-status"><i id="status-dot"></i><span id="status">Loading renderer</span></div><div><span id="sample-count">0</span> <span class="muted">spp</span><span class="separator">·</span><span id="elapsed">0.0</span><span class="muted"> s</span><span class="separator">·</span><span class="muted">CPU / WASM</span></div></div><div class="progress-track"><div id="progress"></div></div></div>
+<aside class="controls"><div class="controls-heading"><h2>Make it your own</h2><p>Same scene. A different atmosphere.</p></div>
+<div class="control-section"><div class="label-row"><h3>SCENE PALETTE</h3><span id="palette-name">The original</span></div><div class="swatches" id="swatches"><span style="--color:#bf4040" title="Left wall"></span><span style="--color:#4040bf" title="Right wall"></span><span style="--color:#bfbfbf" title="Room"></span><span style="--color:#ffffff" title="Mirror sphere"></span><span style="--color:#ffffff" title="Glass sphere"></span></div><button id="randomize" class="primary"><svg><use href="#shuffle"/></svg> Randomize colors <span>↗</span></button><p class="helper">A fresh palette. A new path for every ray.</p></div>
+<div class="control-section quality"><div class="label-row"><label for="samples">RENDER QUALITY</label><span id="quality-label">Balanced</span></div><div class="select-wrap"><select id="samples"><option value="16">16 samples / pixel · Quick</option><option value="64" selected>64 samples / pixel</option><option value="256">256 samples / pixel · Fine</option></select></div><p class="helper">More samples, less noise. Good things take rays.</p></div>
+<div class="scene-details"><div><span>Resolution</span><b>640 × 480</b></div><div><span>Integrator</span><b>Path tracing</b></div><div><span>Materials</span><b>Diffuse, mirror, glass</b></div></div>
+<button id="save" class="secondary"><svg><use href="#download"/></svg> Save image <span>.png</span></button><button id="reset-scene" class="reset"><svg><use href="#reset"/></svg> Reset to original scene</button><div class="privacy"><span>◈</span> All the magic happens on your device.</div>
+</aside></section>
+<section class="features"><article><span class="feature-icon purple"><svg><use href="#code"/></svg></span><div><h3>Tiny by design</h3><p>Kevin Beason’s 99-line renderer.<br/>Small enough to understand. Big enough to inspire.</p></div></article><article><span class="feature-icon amber">☼</span><div><h3>Real light. Real physics.</h3><p>Global illumination, soft shadows, reflections.<br/>Every pixel is a little Monte Carlo experiment.</p></div></article><article><span class="feature-icon green">↯</span><div><h3>Native code. Browser freedom.</h3><p>Compiled from C++ to WebAssembly.<br/>No installs. No uploads. Just your CPU and light.</p></div></article></section>
+<footer><span>A browser experiment, powered by <a href="https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">smallpt by Kevin Beason <svg><use href="#arrow"/></svg></a></span><span class="footer-right">Built with curiosity <span>✳</span> Rendered with patience.</span></footer>
+</main><script is:inline type="module" src="/studio.js"></script>
